'''''Dianthus hyssopifolius''''', the '''fringed pink''' (a name it shares with ''[[Dianthus superbus]]''), is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Caryophyllaceae]].<ref name="DINMO" >{{cite web |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/DINMO |title=''Dianthus hyssopifolius'' (DINMO) |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2023 |website=EPPO Global Database |publisher=European and Mediterranean Plant Protection Organization |access-date=18 December 2023 }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |title=Taxonomy of ''Dianthus'' (Caryophyllaceae) – overall phylogenetic relationships and assessment of species diversity based on a first comprehensive checklist of the genus |date=2022 |last1=Fassou |first1=Georgia |last2=Korotkova |first2=Nadja |last3=Nersesyan |first3=Anush |last4=Koch |first4=Marcus A. |last5=Dimopoulos |first5=Panayotis |last6=Borsch |first6=Thomas |journal=PhytoKeys |issue=196 |pages=91–214 |doi=10.3897/phytokeys.196.77940 |doi-access=free |pmid=36762028 |pmc=9849041 }}</ref> It is native to Portugal, Spain, and France, and it has been introduced to Great Britain.<ref name="POWO_153459-1" >{{cite POWO |id=153459-1 |title=''Dianthus hyssopifolius'' L. |access-date=18 December 2023 }}</ref> A subshrub, it is available from commercial suppliers.<ref name="RHS_301000" >{{cite web |title=''Dianthus hyssopifolius'' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/301000/dianthus-hyssopifolius/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=18 December 2023 |quote=4 suppliers }}</ref>

==Subtaxa==
The following subspecies are accepted:<ref name=" POWO_153459-1" />
*''Dianthus hyssopifolius'' subsp. ''gallicus'' {{small|(Pers.) M.Laínz & Muñoz Garm}} – Spain, France, introduced to Great Britain; called the Jersey pink<ref name="GBIF_3812449" >{{cite web |title=''Dianthus gallicus'' Pers. |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/3812449 |website=gbif.org |publisher=GBIF Secretariat |author=GBIF Backbone Taxonomy |access-date=18 December 2023 }}</ref>
*''Dianthus hyssopifolius'' subsp. ''hyssopifolius'' – Portugal, Spain, France 

